(Bug #131, position 3: a text declared from a call is a text, whether the
 call is written directly or with arguments, so `append` takes it as a
 buffer source like any other text.)

a buffer called sink is "".

To 'make line'.
    Return a text, "made".

To 'make word' with a number called count.
    Return a text, "-word".

a text called word is 'make line'.
append word to sink.
Print sink.

The next is 'make word' of 1.
append next to sink.
Print sink.

The last is 'make line'.
append last to sink.
Print sink.

a text called later is "".
Set later to 'make line'.
append later to sink.
Print sink.
